{% doc %}
  Answers the MCP engine's question "must a proposed change wait for a person?"
  from the desk's own setting, so support admins decide it in the desk rather
  than someone editing an instance constant.

  The setting is `mcp_require_approval`. It is missing until an admin changes
  it, and missing means ON: a desk that has never thought about this gets the
  safe answer, and only an explicit false turns the gate off.

  The engine reads this on every call (queries/approval/enforced), so a change
  takes effect on the next request.
{% enddoc %}
{% liquid
  function settings = 'modules/support/helpers/settings'
  assign out = { "enforced": true }
  if settings.mcp_require_approval == false
    assign out['enforced'] = false
  endif
  return out
%}
